        connection object and return True. When you are done with the
        connection call Gio.DBusConnection.close() and give up your
        reference. Note that the other peer may disconnect at any time -
        a typical thing to do when accepting a connection is to listen to
        the Gio.DBusConnection.closed signal.

        If Gio.DBusServer.props.flags contains Gio.DBusServerFlags.RUN_IN_THREAD
        then the signal is emitted in a new thread dedicated to the
        connection. Otherwise the signal is emitted in the thread-default
        main context (see GLib.MainContext.push_thread_default())
        of the thread that server was constructed in.

