        """Sets or clears self's check-cancellable flag. If this is True
        (the default), then Gio.Task.propagate_pointer(), etc, and
        Gio.Task.had_error() will check the task's Gio.Cancellable first, and
        if it has been cancelled, then they will consider the task to have
        returned an "Operation was cancelled" error
        (Gio.IOErrorEnum.CANCELLED), regardless of any other error or return
        value the task may have had.

